    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "recover refuses a code that does not canonicalise itself (`!canon` beside `!ok`), and so does newRecoveryCodes; and the empty guess this would let through matches no hash hashPassword can write (AUDIT-PW P1 refuses to hash nothing). Kept so the match says what it answers for a non-code without leaning on either caller"
  },
  {
    "name": "RS-a-longer-set-read-short",
    "file": "server-account/src/password.js",
    "old": "Array.from({ length: Math.max(RECOVERY_SET_SIZE, set?.length ?? 0) }",
    "new": "Array.from({ length: RECOVERY_SET_SIZE }",
    "tests": [
      "test/server/recoveryset.test.js"
    ],
    "equivalent": true,
    "why": "no writer makes a set longer than eight (register, newRecoveryCodes and a recovery's fresh set mint RECOVERY_SET_SIZE; a recovery writes fewer). Kept so a longer set, were one ever written, is still read whole and at the same work for every slot"
  }
